      "text_raw": "A folded cascode contains\ntwo DC current sources.\nThe top one, with transistor\nM3, distributes the DC cur-\nrents over both stages. The\nother one acts as an active\nload.\nThe noise of the top cur-\nrent source is very similar\nas for an active load.\nTransistor M3 must be\ndesigned with large V −\nGS\nV or small W/L. Indeed,\nT\nthe full expression shows the\nsame g ratio as for a single-\nm\ntransistor amplifier with\nactive load.\nThe noise of the cascode can be neglected altogether, as shown previously. Its noise is reduced\nby the gain of the input transistor.\nA folded cascode is a low-noise amplifier, provided the noise of transistor M3 can be reduced\nby proper sizing or other techniques.",
      "text": "A folded cascode contains two DC current sources. The top one, with transistor M3, distributes the DC currents over both stages. The other one acts as an active load. The noise of the top current source is very similar as for an active load. Transistor M3 must be designed with large V − GS V or small W/L. Indeed, T the full expression shows the same g ratio as for a singlem transistor amplifier with active load. The noise of the cascode can be neglected altogether, as shown previously. Its noise is reduced by the gain of the input transistor. A folded cascode is a low-noise amplifier, provided the noise of transistor M3 can be reduced by proper sizing or other techniques."
    }
